@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Experimental Vortex build integration
+
+`CUDF_NDSH_WITH_VORTEX=ON` enables the pinned Vortex dependency for Q1 and Q6 only.
+It defaults to `OFF`: ordinary builds neither fetch Vortex nor require Rust.
+This is build scaffolding; the benchmarks still read Parquet until the Vortex
+reader/writer adapter is added.
+
+In a configured RAPIDS development environment, from the repository root:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S cpp -B cpp/build-vortex -G Ninja \
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF -DBUILD_BENCHMARKS=ON \
+  -DCUDF_NDSH_WITH_VORTEX=ON \
+  -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=90
+cmake --build cpp/build-vortex --target NDSH_VORTEX_BUILD_SMOKE --parallel 2
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_VORTEX_BUILD_SMOKE
+cmake --build cpp/build-vortex --target NDSH_Q06_NVBENCH NDSH_Q01_NVBENCH --parallel 2
+```
+
+`90` targets Hopper; choose the architecture for your GPU. To use a local,
+complete Vortex checkout, also pass
+`-DFETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_VORTEX=/absolute/path/to/vortex` at configure time.
+The default fetch is pinned to Vortex commit
+`bffdca1109e99e6957ea2fc18f4a7809c88e0a0c`.
+
+Additional requirements and limitations:
+
+- Linux, Rust 1.95+, and libclang are required. Cargo and the CUDA build scripts
+  download uncached dependencies. Set `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS` to limit Rust parallelism;
+  CMake's `--parallel` does not limit Cargo.
+- Use one toolkit consistently through `CMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER` and
+  `CUDAToolkit_ROOT`. Cargo-owned NVCC invocations do not currently inherit
+  `CMAKE_CUDA_HOST_COMPILER`; set `NVCC_CCBIN` to the same compiler when needed.
+  Check Conda's `NVCC_PREPEND_FLAGS` for conflicting compiler settings.
+- Vortex tests/examples stay disabled, avoiding another nanoarrow dependency.
+  Only the CUDA-enabled Rust FFI archive is linked, through `Vortex::cpp_static`.
+- The smoke target checks cuDF, the Vortex C++ wrapper, and CUDA-session
+  initialization in one process. It does not validate decoding or CUB/nvCOMP
+  execution, which load lazily.
+- Vortex currently builds its own CUB helper and downloads nvCOMP 5.1.0.21 for
+  CUDA 12 independently of cuDF's nvCOMP. Keep the Vortex Cargo build tree intact:
+  these runtime libraries are not packaged by this POC. Successful linking does
+  not establish relocatable deployment or nvCOMP coexistence.
+- Use `RelWithDebInfo` for a symbolized host build. Vortex maps it to Cargo's
+  `release_debug` profile; device line information can be enabled with
+  `NVCC_APPEND_FLAGS=-lineinfo`.
diff --git a/cpp/benchmarks/ndsh/vortex.cmake b/cpp/benchmarks/ndsh/vortex.cmake
